STARTER Configurable Service
============================

1. OVERVIEW
===========

starter-configurable-service (STCS) is a STARTER satellite that turns an XML
configuration into a running bridge between the outside world and
starter-core inputs/outputs.

Data flows through a pipeline of plugins:

  transport  →  reader  →  datapoint (+ transforms)  →  ST input
  ST output  →  datapoint  →  writer  →  transport

For the full technical manual, build the PDF with:

    $ make doc

(also: make -C doc info).

2. PREREQUISITES
================

* GLib 2.0 / GObject / GIO / GModule (libglib2.0-dev)
* starter-core (pkg-config: starter-core)
* libxml2 (libxml2-dev)
* json-glib (libjson-glib-dev)
* libsoup 3.x or 2.4 >= 2.58 (libsoup-3.0-dev or libsoup2.4-dev)
* Autotools (autoconf, automake, libtool)
* Texinfo (makeinfo) to build the manual

3. BUILDING FROM SOURCE
=======================

    $ ./autogen.sh
    $ ./configure
    $ make
    $ sudo make install

4. RUNNING
==========

    $ starter-configurable-service --config /path/to/service.xml

See the manual and the samples under examples/space-track/,
examples/shelly-ht/, and examples/current-time/ for the configuration
language. The current-time example also builds and installs a small
helper binary used by process-transport.

